      "writtenOn": "2022-03-18T21:39:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "After looking through this again, I think here is a potential tricky race that I didn\u0027t handle properly:\nIf the notify_media_capability_remove happens right after notify_media_capability_added and the actual device added message hasn\u0027t been sent out. We\u0027ll lost the removal call and still add the device.\nA proper message queue can solve the problem but requires more work. An alternative way will be replacing the device_added with a hashmap with status enum like \"PendingAdded\", \"Added\" that be also feasible.",
      "parentUuid": "0b96d4c2_db701e25",
      "revId": "1c5d25c86dfd999cbff5591d795f591109d0d0f5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6f976684_607f18fb",
        "filename": "system/gd/rust/linux/stack/src/bluetooth_media.rs",
